meta {
  name: GPS delete - refuses when ENABLE_GPS_EDIT is unset
  type: http
  seq: 45
}

delete {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/gps
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:query {
  deviceId: 08:D1:F9:C8:4D:24
}

docs {
  No time window at all, so this trips the env gate first.

  Expect 403: GPS editing is disabled on this server.
  If your local server has ENABLE_GPS_EDIT=true in .env, expect 400
  instead (see delete-no-window.bru) — that is the next guard, not a
  failure of this check.

  There is no auth in this app (identity is a spoofable MAC header), so
  the endpoint is refused unless the flag is deliberately enabled. Prod
  keeps working untouched until it is.
}
